    <node id="&quot;PROPOLIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A potent naturally occurring antimicrobial used by bees to sterilize hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"A resinous material collected from tree bark and buds used to seal the hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"A resinous material produced by bees that can clog trap slits."&lt;SEP&gt;"A resinous material produced by bees that can glue hive covers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A resinous mixture produced by bees used for sealing and healing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A resinous substance collected by bees used for filling cracks and reinforcing comb in the hive."&lt;SEP&gt;"A sticky substance collected by bees to seal gaps in hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Propolis is a bee-produced resin with healing properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Propolis is a resinous material collected by bees to seal cracks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Propolis is a resinous substance collected by bees from plants to seal hive crevices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Propolis is a resinous substance collected by bees from tree bark and buds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Propolis is a sticky antimicrobial substance made from plant resins used by bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Propolis is a substance used by cementing bees within the hive."</data>
