      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterial contagion that affects bee larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bacterial disease that historically plagued honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"A disease caused by Paenibacillus larvae characterized by brownish pupal mass."&lt;SEP&gt;"A highly contagious bacterial disease affecting honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hive disease that may be treated with antibiotics."&lt;SEP&gt;"A serious microbial disease affecting honey bee larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"American Foulbrood is a disease affecting bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"American Foulbrood is a disease that affects honey bee hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"American Foulbrood is a serious brood disease caused by spore-forming bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a deadly bacterial disease that kills young bee larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a disease affecting bee larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a disease affecting bees, often treated with antibiotics."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a disease affecting honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a disease organism that can affect bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a disease that affects honey bee brood nests."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a disease that can cause bee colonies to die out."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a disease treated with antibiotics via grease patties."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a hive disease that HopGuard may help treat."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a recognizable honey bee disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"American foulbrood is a serious bacterial disease of bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"An infection that affected beekeeping in previous generations."</data>
