    <node id="&quot;GREEN REVOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A historical period of agricultural intensification that increased dependence on nonrenewable energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A period beginning in the 1940s focused on increasing crop production through technology."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution is a period of agricultural intensification that excluded many subsistence farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution is a period of agricultural transformation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution is a period of chemical-based agriculture intended to prevent starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution is an agricultural approach involving field clearing and fertilizer application."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution provided the tenets for commodity production based on failed philosophical concepts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a movement after World War II to increase crop yields."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a period of agricultural increase using fertilizers and pesticides."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a period of agricultural intensification in the twentieth century."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a period of chemical-based agricultural expansion to feed the world."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a period of fertilizer-intensive approaches to boosting crop yields."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a period of significant increase in agricultural production."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a period of technological advances and biotechnology breakthroughs in agriculture."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Green Revolution was a period of technology-driven agricultural increase."</data>
