    <node id="&quot;THOMAS JEFFERSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A person whose public land surveys created a rectangular grid on the land."&lt;SEP&gt;"The designer of the moldboard plow in 1784."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson had a specific understanding of the relationship between agriculture and democracy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a historical figure and author of a quote regarding government."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a historical figure and emblematic representative of the agrarian mentality."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a historical figure associated with agrarianism and agricultural policy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a historical figure mentioned regarding food choice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a historical figure whose farm journal Brown studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is a historical figure whose vision of agriculture is discussed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is an architect of home architecture mentioned by Borgmann."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is quoted regarding the importance of soil to civilization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson is the subject of a farm book."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson served as president of the United States starting in 1801."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was a US president who favored a society of freehold farmers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was a founding father who wrote about the moral virtues of farming."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was a historical figure who designed water collection systems at Monticello."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was a historical figure who grew cover crops and rotated crops."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was a landowner, politician, diplomat, and president of the United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was a plantation owner who researched European farming practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was the owner of Monticello."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thomas Jefferson was the third president of the United States and author of the Declaration of Independence."</data>
