      <data key="d1">"A parasitic mite that affects honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of mite that parasitizes honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific species of mite that affects honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of mite that parasitizes bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"The official scientific name for the varroa mite."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for Varroa mites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a larger cousin of the tracheal mite and a pest to bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a mite that affects bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a mite that threatens bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a parasite that affects bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a parasitic mite that affects honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a parasitic mite that infests honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a pest that represents a significant challenge to honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a species of mite that parasitizes honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a specific species of varroa mite."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is a specific type of mite."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is the biological threat affecting honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is the scientific name for the parasitic mite."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa destructor is the scientific name for the varroa mite."</data>
