    <node id="&quot;VARROA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mite from Asia that parasitizes European honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of mite that parasitizes honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of parasitic mite that affects bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa are mites that affect bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa are mites that infest honey bee hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa are mites that infest honeybee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa are mites that parasitize honey bee brood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa are mites that parasitize honey bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa are parasites that affect honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa are the mites being targeted by the traps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa is a mite that causes damage to beehives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa is a mite that infest honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa is a parasitic mite that affects honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa is a pest that affects honey bee hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa is a type of mite that infests honey bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa mites are parasites known to spread viruses to bees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa refers to mites that infest bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa refers to the mites that infest bee colonies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Varroa, or Varroa destructor, is a mite that affects the beekeeping industry."</data>
