    <node id="&quot;MAITAKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A common name for Grifola frondosa."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gourmet or medicinal mushroom known as Grifola frondosa."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mushroom species (Grifoloa frondosa) used in cultivation cycles."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mushroom species, Grifola frondosa, whose mycelium on grain smells like cold corn tortillas."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of mushroom grown using sawdust-to-sawdust transfers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of mushroom used in cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of cultivated mushroom known for medicinal properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of mushroom cultivated from resterilized Shiitake substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A wood-loving mushroom species also known as Grifola frondosa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as the Dancing Mushroom, it is associated with a fable about nuns and woodcutters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a fleshy polypore fungus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a medicinal mushroom with antiviral and immunopotentiating properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a mushroom sold as fresh, dried, tablets, and teas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a mushroom that can grow from sawdust blocks or wild oak trees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a mushroom with medicinal properties and culinary uses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a species of mushroom that consumes supplemented sawdust."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a species of mushroom used in production blocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a type of gourmet or medicinal mushroom."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a type of mushroom cultivated using oak."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is a type of mushroom with specific environmental requirements for cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake is the Japanese name for the mushroom Grifola frondosa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake, or Grifola frondosa, is a mushroom with similar growth parameters to Sparassis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maitake, or Grifola frondosa, is a type of polypore mushroom."&lt;SEP&gt;"The common name for Grifola frondosa."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a1f902ab89dda85e8440e5325809943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1569a67f674101fc6ab46edc7442941&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53efe0f6b358f27ba33d23a0418e828&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f716dbb539b9e685559a05a8f9f5d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dffef103751c7f68ca10f94c7362508e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d339b8febe86c1bfb409fde4970989e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc5200861bfbf924cb02074bbc681c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a1f23ac039aa3ef70ba8ce3a43a9117&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4466fc05408f4d774f674142f50ffdd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4be6e62e9f709cb21a7f4bc14f814a83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d305ceab31b27e4602db91f42ba2fe00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71d4b92006db2e1bfffb89c800fc0a3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aea472dfebfe03f6968437bd2ffedd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35b441cca050d846fb6c051fc61db257&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c4109338117a5ad23b02b74d9159c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91456f98a926e6abc80385dc245cc777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7abff67abadea6025485a9d790fcc373&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1c5dbb55ca53672746cb230af692bc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d79cc325ae91205a578658535a12a8d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60e69eb2d86122d16e8c9ec35a897823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a529b2a82aeedaec884d490e181507e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee67735ee2d22fc01623c11e43940a78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1bc36cc5ea2bacf01a722ac6bd8da3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ac66f2a993a8f84ec2280130d78e1c7</data>
