    <node id="&quot;GANODERMA LUCIDUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mushroom species known to produce volunteer primordia on specific media."&lt;SEP&gt;"Also known as Reishi mushrooms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is a fungus species, also known as Reishi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is a fungus that produces secondary metabolites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is a mushroom from which antiviral components have been isolated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is a mushroom suggested to be taken with vitamin C."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is a mushroom whose antler formation is controlled by carbon dioxide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is a species of fungus being cultivated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is a species of mushroom also known as Reishi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is a type mushroom species that grows on oaks and hardwoods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is the scientific name for Reishi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ganoderma lucidum is the scientific name for the Reishi mushroom."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mushroom species known as Reishi."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for Reishi mushrooms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for the Reishi fungus."&lt;SEP&gt;"The scientific name for the Reishi mushroom."</data>
