    <node id="&quot;REISHI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A common name for Ganoderma lucidum."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gourmet or medicinal mushroom known as Ganoderma lucidum."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medicinal mushroom of the species Ganoderma lucidum."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mushroom species (Ganoderma lucidum) used in cultivation cycles."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mushroom species also known as Ganoderma lucidum."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of mushroom grown using sawdust-to-sawdust transfers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A species of mushroom used in cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of cultivated mushroom studied for medicinal benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of fungus, also known as Ganoderma lucidum, being grown in sawdust spawn."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of mushroom cultivated from resterilized Shiitake substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of mushroom used in cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a cultivated mushroom used in medicinal tea."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a medicinal fungus used as a price benchmark for Zhu Ling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a medicinal mushroom used for immunological disorders and cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a medicinal polypore mushroom that fruits in the summer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a mushroom cultivated via shaded logs in Japan and the United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a mushroom grown for medicinal and culinary use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a mushroom often pictured on Zhu Ling labels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a mushroom species that can be grown on logs buried in sawdust or soil."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a mushroom species that demonstrates strong photosensitivity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a polypore mushroom whose recycled blocks are used as substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a species of mushroom used in production blocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a type of fungus used in log culture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a type of mushroom grown in various countries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a type of mushroom mentioned in the context of mycelium appearance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a type of mushroom used in cultivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reishi is a type of mushroom with a dense m